  "statement": "With $O(0,0,0)$, $A(1,1,0)$, $B(1,0,1)$, $C(0,1,1)$, find the volume of the tetrahedron $OABC$.",
  "solution": "Volume $=\\tfrac16|\\vec{OA}\\cdot(\\vec{OB}\\times\\vec{OC})|$. $\\vec{OA}=(1,1,0)$, $\\vec{OB}=(1,0,1)$, $\\vec{OC}=(0,1,1)$. $\\vec{OB}\\times\\vec{OC}=(-1,-1,1)$. Then $\\vec{OA}\\cdot(\\vec{OB}\\times\\vec{OC})=1(-1)+1(-1)+0=-2$. So volume $=\\tfrac16|{-2}|=\\tfrac13$.",
  "hints": [
    "Use the scalar triple product for the parallelepiped volume.",
    "Divide by $6$ for the tetrahedron."
  ],
